================================================================================
  SECTION 5: BUGS FOUND AND FIXED (v5.1 → v6.0)
================================================================================

  [BUG-1] CRITICAL: Battery GUID Conflict (LINE 479-481 in v5.1)
    PROBLEM: Critical battery action GUID 637ea02f was being set to 3 (Hibernate)
             BUT this GUID is actually the Energy Saver threshold, NOT critical action.
             Line 454 also sets the same GUID to 100 — conflict!
             The correct GUID for critical battery action is d8742dcb.
    FIX:     Swapped GUIDs — d8742dcb now gets action=3, 637ea02f gets action=0
    IMPACT:  System would never hibernate on critical battery → deep discharge damage

  [BUG-2] HIGH: PowerToys wildcard taskkill (LINE 1525 in v5.1)
    PROBLEM: taskkill /IM "PowerToys*" — taskkill doesn't support wildcards in /IM
             This silently failed every time, leaving PowerToys processes running
    FIX:     Changed to explicit /FI "IMAGENAME eq PowerToys.exe" per process
    IMPACT:  PowerToys was never actually killed in re-apply mode

  [BUG-3] HIGH: Balanced mode doesn't reset GPU preferences
    PROBLEM: Ultra Performance sets DirectXUserGlobalSettings=GpuPreference=2
             and EnableMsHybrid=2, DisablePowerMizer=1 in registry.
             Balanced mode never clears these — apps keep using RTX 3050
    FIX:     Added step [6/6] in balanced that deletes these registry keys
    IMPACT:  After using Ultra Perf once, GPU was stuck on RTX 3050 until reboot

  [BUG-4] HIGH: Re-apply ignores power source
    PROBLEM: Quick re-apply ([R]) always applies battery saver settings even
             when laptop woke up plugged into AC power
    FIX:     Added CIM battery status check — skips re-apply if on AC
    IMPACT:  User was accidentally throttling CPU to 40% while plugged in

  [BUG-5] MEDIUM: No log rotation
    PROBLEM: PowerOptimizer.log grows unbounded (was 160KB / 2,344 lines)
    FIX:     Added :logrotate subroutine, trims to 500 lines on saver activation
    IMPACT:  Log file would eventually consume significant disk space

  [BUG-6] MEDIUM: Disk space integer overflow
    PROBLEM: set /a uses 32-bit signed integers — drives >2TB show negative
    FIX:     Replaced with PowerShell Get-PSDrive for disk space display
    IMPACT:  Cosmetic — would show wrong values on large drives

  [BUG-7] MEDIUM: Webcam only registry-fixed, not disabled
    PROBLEM: Energy report showed webcam at 0% suspend time. Registry
             SelectiveSuspendEnabled=1 alone wasn't enough.
    FIX:     Now also calls Disable-PnpDevice on webcam in saver mode,
             re-enables in balanced mode
    IMPACT:  Webcam was drawing ~0.5W continuously even in saver

  [BUG-8] LOW: MongoDB auto-restarts after service stop
    PROBLEM: net stop MongoDB stops it, but service is set to auto-start
             so it could restart on its own or after wake
    FIX:     sc config MongoDB start= demand in saver, start= auto in balanced
    IMPACT:  MongoDB's 1ms timer resolution request would return after wake

