================================================================================
  SECTION 9: CRITICAL BUG FOUND AND FIXED (Bluetooth Hardware Kill)
================================================================================

  [BUG-9] CRITICAL: Webcam Disable-PnpDevice kills Bluetooth hardware

    PROBLEM:
      In :saver [13/15], the script called Disable-PnpDevice on the webcam
      device matching *VID_13D3*PID_3563*. This VID/PID matches a USB
      Composite Device — when disabled, it takes down the entire USB
      composite hub including the PHYSICAL BLUETOOTH CONTROLLER.

      Result: Every time Ultra Battery Saver was activated, Bluetooth
      hardware was completely killed. Bluetooth devices (mouse, headphones,
      etc.) would disconnect and could not reconnect until balanced/
      performance mode re-enabled the device.

      This was introduced in v6.0 as [BUG-7] fix (Section 5, line 246).
      The original BUG-7 analysis correctly identified the webcam's 0%
      suspend time but the fix was too aggressive — disabling the device
      rather than just setting the registry key.

    ROOT CAUSE:
      VID_13D3 & PID_3563 corresponds to a USB Composite Device that
      hosts multiple functions on one USB port:
        - Webcam (camera function)
        - Bluetooth controller (radio function)
      Calling Disable-PnpDevice disables the ENTIRE composite device,
      not just the webcam function.

    FIX:
      - REMOVED: Disable-PnpDevice call for *VID_13D3*PID_3563* in :saver
      - KEPT:    SelectiveSuspendEnabled=1 registry modification (safe)
      - REMOVED: Enable-PnpDevice call for *VID_13D3*PID_3563* in :balanced
                 (no longer needed since device is never disabled)
      - UPDATED: All comments, log messages, and summary banners

    IMPACT:  Bluetooth hardware remains functional in all power modes.
             Webcam still benefits from USB Selective Suspend via registry.

  --- CORRECTION TO PREVIOUS LOG ENTRIES ---

    [W3] (Section 3, line 132-137): STATUS changed from
         "FIXED (v6.0) — Device now disabled in saver mode"
         to "FIXED (v6.0) — Selective suspend enabled via registry only.
         Device is NOT disabled (would kill Bluetooth)."

    [BUG-7] (Section 5, line 243-248): PARTIALLY REVERTED.
         The Disable-PnpDevice portion was unsafe and has been removed.
         The SelectiveSuspendEnabled registry fix remains.

